From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: a proxy keeps the security blanket set on it

IClientSecurity on a COM proxy was a stub: SetBlanket, QueryBlanket and
CopyProxy answered E_NOTIMPL, so CoSetProxyBlanket, CoQueryProxyBlanket and
CoCopyProxy failed. Omaha's updaters set a blanket on the proxies of their
COM servers and stop when that fails: Brave's standalone installer put its
updater in place and then reported "Installation failed. Error code:
0x80004001". A proxy manager now keeps one blanket (calls still go over
local RPC, which has no authentication levels to change): setting it checks
its arguments (E_INVALIDARG for an unknown service or level) and that the
interface is the proxy's own remote one (E_NOINTERFACE for its IMarshal),
a query returns it, and a copy is the proxy itself. ole32's tests of this
pass without todo_wine.
---
--- a/dlls/combase/marshal.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/marshal.c
@@ -82,6 +82,10 @@
     HANDLE remoting_mutex;    /* mutex used for synchronizing access to IRemUnknown */
     MSHCTX dest_context;      /* context used for activating optimisations (LOCK) */
     void *dest_context_data;  /* reserved context value (LOCK) */
+    /* the security blanket set through IClientSecurity (CS cs); one for the
+     * whole object rather than one per interface */
+    DWORD authn_svc, authz_svc, authn_level, imp_level, capabilities;
+    WCHAR *server_princ;
 };
 
 static inline struct proxy_manager *impl_from_IMultiQI(IMultiQI *iface)
@@ -1359,6 +1363,23 @@
     return IMultiQI_Release(&This->IMultiQI_iface);
 }
 
+/* Whether iface is one of the proxy's own remote interfaces (or its
+ * controlling IUnknown); the proxy manager's local ones, such as IMarshal,
+ * have no blanket. */
+static BOOL proxy_manager_owns(struct proxy_manager *This, IUnknown *iface)
+{
+    struct ifproxy *ifproxy;
+    BOOL found = FALSE;
+
+    if (!iface) return FALSE;
+    if (iface == (IUnknown *)&This->IMultiQI_iface) return TRUE;
+    EnterCriticalSection(&This->cs);
+    LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(ifproxy, &This->interfaces, struct ifproxy, entry)
+        if (ifproxy->iface == iface) { found = TRUE; break; }
+    LeaveCriticalSection(&This->cs);
+    return found;
+}
